{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/43912-st-advice-how-to-deal-with-cannonites-purists","id":43912,"title":"ST Advice?: How to deal with Cannonites/Purists","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-06T20:15:06-08:00","id":43912,"title":"ST Advice?: How to deal with Cannonites/Purists","content":"So, i was running a quick game of HtR.<br /> was running my game, all nice and dandy to some old HtR players and i use carpenter...and suddenly, a wirld Cannonite/Purist jump saying<br /> &quot;Dude you cant use carpenter, according to the Cannon he Was send into oblivion.&quot;, followed by other player saying &quot;Yeah, the wraith rules stablish that you cant leave the laberynth once you get stuck in it.&quot;<br /> <br /> this isnt the solely related Cannon thing, tried to run a campaing of scion and i keept being shouted &quot;Dude a god would never do that, acording to the old myths he would ally X more likely rather than Y, even if its for temporal alliance.&quot;<br /> <br /> how do you guys deal with guys stuck up with the cannon ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T20:40:28-08:00","id":43924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/43912-st-advice-how-to-deal-with-cannonites-purists#post43912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, i was running a quick game of HtR.<br /> was running my game, all nice and dandy to some old HtR players and i use carpenter...and suddenly, a wirld Cannonite/Purist jump saying<br /> &quot;Dude you cant use carpenter, according to the Cannon he Was send into oblivion.&quot;, followed by other player saying &quot;Yeah, the wraith rules stablish that you cant leave the laberynth once you get stuck in it.&quot;<br /> <br /> this isnt the solely related Cannon thing, tried to run a campaing of scion and i keept being shouted &quot;Dude a god would never do that, acording to the old myths he would ally X more likely rather than Y, even if its for temporal alliance.&quot;<br /> <br /> how do you guys deal with guys stuck up with the cannon ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the time I just ask them to either adapt or leave. Before I start playing with anyone new I tell him or her what's what. If he doesn't like it, then I'll gladly lead them to the door.<br /> I had really bad experiences both as player and as an ST with canon adherence, so i actively try to inform everyone about my stance before I start to play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To a player who wanted his character to attend a very &quot;special&quot; school:<br /> There is no Charles F. Lupus school for gifted werewolves.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/971-arag","name":"Arag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar971_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T20:51:29-08:00","id":43931,"title":"","content":"funny enough, i did. they said &quot;Yeah no prob.&quot;<br /> <br /> and then shit hit the fan","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T21:08:58-08:00","id":43941,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">You know those foam pool noodles? I took a piece of one, duct-taped to a plastic pipe and created\u2026<i>The Ret-Con Gavel of Doooooooom!</i><br /> <br /> Among other things, I used it whenever a canon question up. If I deemed it inappropriate or stupid, I ruled thus: <i>\u201cYour disagreement has been ruled as canon-fodder [play on words &lt;giggles&gt;]!! The gavel has spoken!!\u201d</i> And I would pound it on whatever corebook we were using three times. <br /> <br /> This mighty power was only used when players would go out of their ways to be annoying about bits of story-stuff and lore. It was never used to sabotage a character, just to shut up a player. As Arag said, tell them to deal or leave. Pointless arguments about whose mother did what with whom in some random source book is\u2026vexing. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T01:44:19-08:00","id":44030,"title":"","content":"Yeah, especially when its usually centered on fluff or game world's fiction; which often tend to be of only mediocre quality even at best, and usually those canon nazis aren't even interested about RAW making their arguments rather childish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1700-blue-fox","name":"Blue Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T01:50:12-08:00","id":44032,"title":"","content":"I'm fortunate in most of the folks I play with don't lean that way. However, I do have an official policy in this area:<br /> <br /> The games I run are in <i>my</i> world. This is a version of the world in the books, but is in no way guaranteed to be exactly the same as the whole canon universe. Any deviations that you would know in-character I will make you aware of before the game begins. Any deviations in material that your characters wouldn't know about is fair game. For example, you do not know what the True Brujah are, what Disciplines they have, or how those Disciplines works. If I decide to include one, I am under no obligation to keep it canon. You know how Gangrel and Protean work, so I'll tell you in advance if I intend to house-rule them.<br /> <br /> Further, I'm not an encyclopedia, nor do I own every single WoD book ever printed. If something was written about in a book I haven't read, <b>it probably doesn't exist</b>.<br /> <br /> Finally, and most importantly, the ST's word is law. To make a Storyteller game work, you make an agreement. The ST will do a crapload of work to prepare and run game, and the players show to get an evening of free entertainment. In exchange for this fantastic deal, you understand that it's the ST's show. If I say that a dude name Carpenter shows up, roll with it. If I say that the rules are going to work a certain way, that's how they work. I'm always open to advice and constructive criticism (and have been known to change my mind as a result of such), but ultimately when I make a call at the gaming table I expect it to be respected and the discussion to end. That's the deal. Players need to give their ST enough trust and authority to run a game, and things break down if they try to revoke that at every turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>Demon Cat</b></span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://flamingporcupine.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Illuminated Dark Ages character sheets and more</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10-demon-cat","name":"Demon Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"266"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T04:30:38-08:00","id":44072,"title":"","content":"While I agree with the other posts I would like to point out that your canon purist friend is actually wrong about Carpenter. First off in <i>The Walking Dead</i> Carpenter went through a Harrowing, there's no indication that he failed it nor does a failed Harrowing automatically turn a wraith into a spectre. Second save for destruction or spectre transformation, the outcomes of a Harrowing include the wraith being tossed from the Labyrinth and returned to one of their fetters. Third Carpenter did return from that, appearing as a major character in the MtR trilogy and again in the ToJ ticker where it was mentioned that the tombstone of the woman who betrayed him had been smashed with a hammer, his second known fetter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T05:28:49-08:00","id":44094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/43912-st-advice-how-to-deal-with-cannonites-purists#post43912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, i was running a quick game of HtR.<br /> was running my game, all nice and dandy to some old HtR players and i use carpenter...and suddenly, a wirld Cannonite/Purist jump saying<br /> &quot;Dude you cant use carpenter, according to the Cannon he Was send into oblivion.&quot;, followed by other player saying &quot;Yeah, the wraith rules stablish that you cant leave the laberynth once you get stuck in it.&quot;<br /> <br /> this isnt the solely related Cannon thing, tried to run a campaing of scion and i keept being shouted &quot;Dude a god would never do that, acording to the old myths he would ally X more likely rather than Y, even if its for temporal alliance.&quot;<br /> <br /> how do you guys deal with guys stuck up with the cannon ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Two weeks ago a player asked me<br /> (A): How many seconds is a round?<br /> (ME): Six seconds per round<br /> Another player charge in<br /> (B): 4 seconds<br /> (ME): 6 seconds<br /> (B): The manual say 4 seconds<br /> (ME): I don't remember, but from now on it's 6 seconds<br /> (B): But in the manual...<br /> (ME): Don't compel me to write on my own book.<br /> (B): <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And that's it.<br /> <br /> It's your game, even if it's not totally canon you're the storyteller<br /> you can even resolve that the Hunters get their powers from Saulot (ehi, that's a cool story....), and if you can storytell it good, it will still be a good game<br /> <br /> but make it clear that it's <u>your</u> game, and the to hell the canon","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":515,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","user":"Ryoga84","date":". 01-07-2014, 08:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T05:53:43-08:00","id":44101,"title":"","content":"One thing I will say - from the point of view of someone who agreed to play a V:tM game because of the setting - the small stuff doesn't matter. Oh, sure Carpenter did whatever to whoever in book whogivesaflyingfuck.<br /> <br /> But if it's <i>your</i> world Mr. ST then <i>please</i> tell me how your differs in advance and be ready to answer my (probably many) questions about how it now operates and give me the leeway to change my actions and responses (and maybe even retroactively edit) if your changes are big enough to affect a setting point.<br /> <br /> As much as he's a good GM the V:tM guy who runs the games just kills it by making it very much <i>his</i> world. It can be a long train of frustration trying to build or play a character with connections to the setting or to have expectations about how things should work or to make assumptions about how people might respond etc. It's playing in a world where you can't really make informed decisions - or at least not decisions informed by the game material.<br /> <br /> Generally though? I agreed to play Vampire the Masquerade, not Vampire the Bastardising.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T07:59:32-08:00","id":44168,"title":"","content":"Well, the ST can hardly be asked to go through every person in the Canon and state whether or not he changed some thing about that person.<br /> <br /> And this is far from Vampire the Bastardizing. This is a very minor change to one character. It's not like vampires are all of a sudden glittering or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T08:51:32-08:00","id":44198,"title":"","content":"I think the best way is to make sure that everyone is on the same field at the start of the game. So maybe mention that you won't play by all the rules writen and will change some stuff to keep it interesting. Or that the game will be puritan in regards to canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T09:03:51-08:00","id":44213,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I have a blanket understanding in any game that I run that I may be inspired by the metaplot, but the game itself is not part of it. So in a recent Changeling: The Dreaming game, for example, my players didn't bat an eye when High King David showed up mind controlled by House Balor in a plot to free the Formorians from their eternal prison <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T09:27:09-08:00","id":44231,"title":"","content":"This rule is in every WoD core book, but I'll quote the one from W:tA Revised:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>The Golden Rule</b><br /> This rule is the most important one, and it\u2019s the only rule worth following to the letter: There are no rules. None that you must adhere to, that is. If you don\u2019t like it, change it. We have tried to create a simple system that can be used to simulate the complex varieties of life (and obviously, we think it works fine for that). However, there\u2019s no accounting for the creativity of the human condition. Not all of our rules will work well in your stories, so mix them up. Run a whole session without using any dice. Or spread out the map and run a tactical version of the attack on the warehouse. Do whatever you like. This book is nothing more than a collection of guidelines, suggestions and ideas. The rules are ways of helping you capture the essence of the World of Darkness in a game format. But these rules are only to help, not to restrict. Whatever works best for you is the right way to go. We have given you the tools, now go make whatever you want out of<br /> them. p.175 <u>W:tA Revised</u> </div> </div> </div>For us, not only does this affect the mechanics, but the setting as well.<br /> <br /> We called this &quot;Rule 69&quot; because we were teens, and it was on page 69 of some book once upon a time, but basically it gives the ST the right (and duty) to fuck any rule for the pleasure of the players and the story they deem necessary. <br /> <br /> NOW, I agree that if a player builds a character with certain mechanics in mind, that the ST should inform players that there's a change in those mechanics ahead of time. Also, if there is some major change to the world/story that a character would understand as being a certain way, then the ST should try to make those changes known (The Shadow Lords are the Kings of the Garou in my game, The Sabbat have made a truce in this city, Virtual Adepts have returned to the Technocracy, The Red Star hasn't shown up yet, etc.) However, if the ST decides that the PCs are going to walk into a bar and see someone who the canon says should be dead, and those characters don't know who it is/have association with that?... then it is fully within the STs right to continue to mess with the canon because it shouldn't matter to the story. Holy fuck! Sam Haight's still alive and living on the down-low in Hartford Connecticut? There's probably going to be a fun story to be had then! The ST can change his powers even! The rumors of Haight's demise must have been false! (even though canon says otherwise.)<br /> <br /> I've played with Rules Nazis who can't handle changes in mechanics from the book (especially when their &quot;concepts&quot; don't make any sense but were made to min-max powers), but we've rarely ever played with Canon Nazis because, well, most of our STs have NEVER followed strict canon to any game (even Star Wars.)<br /> <br /> However, if you know that these people are going to be this way in your games, just let them know up front &quot;This will not be a Canon Game, and if you're comfortable with that, then you can play.&quot; Otherwise, don't let them ruin your game by being dicks to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T09:56:20-08:00","id":44254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HOD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/43912-st-advice-how-to-deal-with-cannonites-purists?p=44168#post44168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the ST can hardly be asked to go through every person in the Canon and state whether or not he changed some thing about that person.<br /> <br /> And this is far from Vampire the Bastardizing. This is a very minor change to one character. It's not like vampires are all of a sudden glittering or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did say I didn't care about some random character in some random book.<br /> <br /> I said I was convinced to play the game because of the setting.<br /> <br /> If you change the setting (Clan doesn't exist, Caine is a lie, Gehenna is not a thing, Tremere are the premier clan in the Camarilla (I think they're the GMs favourite so they tend to be in charge of everything or end up as the real power, etc.) I deserve to know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T11:35:43-08:00","id":44317,"title":"","content":"Give them the 2-point flaw &quot;Twisted Upbringing&quot;. Then, any time they say &quot;But that's not canon!&quot;, you can tell them their parents lied to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T11:45:12-08:00","id":44324,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/43912-st-advice-how-to-deal-with-cannonites-purists?p=44317#post44317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Give them the 2-point flaw &quot;Twisted Upbringing&quot;. Then, any time they say &quot;But that's not canon!&quot;, you can tell them their parents lied to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is just completely evil. I'll cite you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;</span>Explanations exist; they have existed for all time; there is always a well-known solution to every human problem \u2014 neat, plausible, and wrong.<span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;<br /> - H.L. Mencken</span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/467-bob-the-skull","name":"Bob the Skull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar467_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T15:52:08-08:00","id":44493,"title":"","content":"I make it clear to my players that I <i>heavily</i> edit any and all settings that I run, and the only part of those changes they're guaranteed to be informed of up front are the ones that would impact character generation (including cluing them in on any changes that would impact &quot;secret&quot; parts of their backstory). And if they don't like it, they can walk.<br /> <br /> When they ask me why I mod everything so heavily, I go through the following reasons<br /> - To save them from the temptation to Metagame. If nothing they've read is <i>guaranteed</i> to be accurate, it actually <i>frees</i> me to use <i>more</i> elements of the setting that a well-read player is intimately familiar with.<br /> - A lot of the stuff that's in the books is incoherent, or incomplete, or just plain goofy. I will not use flawed material if I can generate something better. Of course, I often <i>can't</i> generate something better, which is why I still ran so much Exalted 2E, even with its deeply flawed mechanics.<br /> - Sometimes stuff in the books is inoffensive, but still incompatible with my plans.<br /> - Sometimes stuff in the books is incompatible with <i>other stuff in other books</i>, and picking one part means I'm trashing another. See: CWoD Crossover games.<br /> - I'm an arrogant son of a bitch, and I've interacted with enough RPG writers not to hold &quot;canon&quot; in any particular reverence, unless the I find the specific material particularly inspiring. So sometimes I mod things because I <i>can</i> mod things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please add signature.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/615-the-hanged-man","name":"The Hanged Man","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T19:34:00-08:00","id":47810,"title":"","content":"Most of us have had to deal with a canon-stickler at some point. In my venue sheets, I put a big disclaimer in that not only do I reserve the right to change canon, I consider it an <i>obligation</i>. There's no way in hell that any character would know everything about the World of Darkness, so I'm really doing the players a favor by enhancing the mystique and unknowns of the setting.<br /> <br /> One of my favorite canon changes is to re-jigger the exact nature of the Sabbat--since I run mostly Camarilla games, I want to keep the Sabbat scary and unknown. I've rarely ran the Sabbat exactly as they're presented in the books, and I think the games have been more compelling for it.<br /> <br /> For what it's worth, the issue of &quot;canon enthusiasts&quot; is one I've not had too many issues with in the World of Darkness. It's absolutely horrible among people that want to play any version of the Star Wars RPG... One of the main reasons that I've never kept a Star Wars game going long-term. It used to be pretty bad for D&amp;D players in the Forgotten Realms setting, but it seems to have calmed down in the past decade or so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/902-dykstrav","name":"Dykstrav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T22:20:53-08:00","id":47927,"title":"","content":"I was going to site a video I found by user Hammereshitsteak exploring the Virtues and Vices of roleplayers where he discusses the rules lawyers and purists, but apparently that vid has been taken down. So I'll just second the ST gavel of Doom Method. Though my ST gavel is just plastic and less impressive. It still gets the point across. I let players have a chance to convince me why I am not allowed to do something out of cannon using cannon plots, but should I deem them overruled, my decision is final. So sayeth the gavel. If your players are willing to leave your table over it, let them, they either A. Don't have enough information from you as to why they should suspend that disbelief, or B. they have a habit of questioning your authority and are willing to call your bluff to get their way. The solution is an open line of communication. You and your players need to be able to talk through a disagreement. An ST needs to be able to ask their players to have faith in them to make a good story even if the books lay events out differently, but the ST also has to give the players a chance to give constructive criticism. The players need to trust their ST, but also be willing to accept that the ST's word is the last word, and while they might not agree with a ruling, they should give it a chance to see how it plays out. It's all a part of a game. Take a step back and breathe. Then be objective. In the end, it's all about making a good story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T07:31:32-08:00","id":48152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/43912-st-advice-how-to-deal-with-cannonites-purists?p=44317#post44317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Give them the 2-point flaw &quot;Twisted Upbringing&quot;. Then, any time they say &quot;But that's not canon!&quot;, you can tell them their parents lied to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>BEST! ANSWER! <b>EVER!</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T10:10:52-08:00","id":48282,"title":"","content":"I'm going to take a bit of a dissenting voice here: it's not just the STs game - players and the ST own the game together and should be collaborating. If you've got a canon buff in your game throwing a strop, ask them why the change bothers them. It also sounds to me like there's more involved here than just one minor change. Was there anything else leading up to this or was it an isolated incident? Similarly was it necessary to use Carpenter rather than a Carpenter-equivalent? :/<br /> <br /> Generally, when I'm a player, I hate unexpected deviation from canon unless there's a good reason for it. Usually (in my experience) its a warning sign that the ST isn't familiar enough with the material they're using to keep it consistent (&quot;You meet Sam Haight&quot; &quot;The bloodthirsty wolfskinning lunatic?&quot; &quot;Nah, my Sam Haight is a peaceful gardener&quot;) or considers the setting that was agreed on with the players too boring and is trying to spice it up somehow without really thinking things through (&quot;The Prince of the city is a Lasombra&quot; &quot;oh, that's weird&quot; &quot;not really. In my game Lasombra are the Ventrue and Ventrue are the Lasombra&quot; &quot;why?&quot; &quot;because it's more interesting&quot;).<br /> <br /> In contrast, if I'm told from the get-go that the ST is planning on making Brujah purple, Toreador blue and the plot'll run fast and loose with canon, I'll be much happier. Why? Because it shows forethought and I can be fairly confident there's a payoff down the line for it - the changes are made for a reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1984,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1984-crivrev","user":"CrivRev","date":". 01-13-2014, 01:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1984-crivrev","name":"CrivRev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T13:46:55-08:00","id":52732,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://funnyasduck.net/wp-content/uploads/2012/12/funny-no-seagulls-sign-bird-call-cops-dont-give-fuck-pics.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T21:12:32-08:00","id":55927,"title":"","content":"The main thing I make sure of in any game I play in or run is consisitancy. If you're going to run a game where you change the rules or setting then you have to inform your group what those changes are and then stick to them. Nothing will cause me to quit a game faster than inconsistent rules, especially if power a does one thing for players but something totally different for npcs. If I have a character with power A and you decide that power no longer works as written, then when an NPC uses the same power you can't decide that all the sudden it does work as written. I hold myself to that rule when running games, and I expect whoever I game with will follow that rule as well. As long as that's the case I'm usually good with any changes. <br /> <br /> \u200bOh, and if you're a &quot;my way or the highway&quot; sort, I'll take the highway every time. Gaming is about a shared experience and everyone having fun together, not being lorded over. Talk with your players and find a balance that your group as a whole agrees will be fun. Without finding a balance you'll wind up with no one wanting to game with you. I suppose it all boils down to &quot;Don't be a dick&quot;, which applies to both players and storytellers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I'm immortal, I've been right so far&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/301-bwchism","name":"bwchism","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar301_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}